# M55 Scope-Aware Repository Preflight

Normative authority:

- `docs/ssot/M55_SCOPE_AWARE_REPO_PREFLIGHT_SSOT.md`
- `docs/ssot/M55_GIT_FIRST_HARDENING_SSOT.md`
- `docs/ssot/M55_GIT_PREFLIGHT_MANIFEST.json`

Before substantive M55 work, establish task-relevant Git identity. Then classify the task into exactly one profile:

- `FULL_REPO_PREFLIGHT`
- `CONTINUATION_FAST_PATH`
- `PINNED_REVIEW_PREFLIGHT`

## Hard trigger — AI self-classification cannot bypass

`HARD_TRIGGER_FORCES_FULL_PREFLIGHT = TRUE`

If intended or observed mutation touches any of these semantic/path families, force `FULL_REPO_PREFLIGHT`:

- `docs/ssot/**`
- `.product-authority/**`
- `lib/m55/contracts/**`
- `app/api/stripe/**`
- checkout or webhook API code
- `supabase/**`, migrations, DB schema/RPC/RLS/privileges
- Creator commission/ledger/payout/tax/provider policy
- `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/**`, or control/security/release workflows
- `M55_EXECUTION_STATE.json`
- money, price, commission rate, reward, legal/tax, identity/KYC, security, attribution/ledger authority, provider behavior, cross-lane ownership

On a hard trigger, FAST is prohibited even if the task looks editorial or small.

## CONTINUATION_FAST_PATH

Use for an already-authorized bounded continuation lane such as UIUX only when lane, mutation owner, worktree/ref, gate/task family, mutable scope, and semantics remain unchanged and no hard trigger enters scope.

Do not force unrelated Creator Revenue, Stripe payout, Japan legal/tax, or global repo archaeology onto a valid UIUX continuation merely because those programs exist elsewhere.

A fresh `origin/main` reconciliation is not required every turn. Require it before merge/sync integration, when touched-path/shared-authority drift is relevant, or when another escalation trigger occurs.

FAST_PATH is fast, not blind: task-relevant Git identity and lane authority are still mandatory.

## FULL_REPO_PREFLIGHT

Escalate before new architecture/economics/reward/legal/tax/provider/security/DB/ledger/payout/SSOT/governance/roadmap decisions, cross-lane integration, unknown existing-contract coverage, hard-trigger mutation, or consequential new GREEN/freeze/authorization.

Minimum full evidence is bounded to relevant authority: `AGENTS.md`, `M55_EXECUTION_STATE.json`, fresh remote main, SSOT index, relevant normative SSOTs, relevant unmerged PR/stacked authority, relevant CLOSED/no-replay evidence, and local identity when local mutation is proposed.

Search existing SSOT before creating a new contract. Chat memory alone is insufficient for consequential M55 architecture.

## PINNED_REVIEW_PREFLIGHT

For read-only independent review, pin exact PR/branch/commit, exact diff/artifact boundary, relevant lane authority, accepted baselines, and mutation prohibition. Do not load unrelated business/global SSOTs unless the diff touches them.

## Lane lock before mutation

`LANE_LOCK_REQUIRED_BEFORE_MUTATION = TRUE`

Use fresh branch/worktree/HEAD/status plus `M55_WORKTREE_REGISTRY.md` ownership and the exact mutable-path allowlist. A future `.m55_lane_state.json` may be used only as a generated cache; it never overrides the registry or fresh Git evidence.

Any lane-owner mismatch, allowlist violation, or ownership ambiguity is STOP.

Do not mutate existing protected UIUX worktrees merely to add lane-state markers.

## Context refresh

At a material subtask boundary, re-enter the Git-first flow and reselect FAST/REVIEW/FULL. A new chat is optional and is never authority or a CLOSED-GREEN invalidator.

`SUBTASK_BOUNDARY_CONTEXT_REFRESH_REQUIRED = TRUE`

## Escalation triggers

Escalate FAST_PATH to FULL on any of:

- any hard trigger above;
- new Human architecture/economic/reward decision;
- legal/tax/provider/DB/ledger/security/governance semantics;
- cross-lane authority collision;
- relevant unmerged authority;
- relevant main/authority drift;
- unknown existing-contract coverage;
- new consequential PLAN/DESIGN GREEN or freeze.

A main SHA change by itself is not a global stop. Determine relevance to the lane first.

One lane's FULL preflight must not globally block unrelated valid continuation lanes.
